{"id": "P06855", "name": "John H. MacMillan IV IV", "name_chinese": "", "country": "United States", "net_worth_usd_m": "1069.0", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time", "source_of_wealth": "Cargill", "industry": "food & beverage", "sec_insider_companies": "", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (2026)", "focus": [], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/john-h-macmillan-iv-iv/", "wikidata_url": "", "forbes_bio": ["John G. MacMillan IV is one of 21 billionaire heirs to Cargill, America's largest private company.", "His great-grandfather, W.W. Cargill, founded the business as a single grain warehouse on the end of an Iowa railroad line in 1865.", "The family still owns roughly 90% of Cargill, which did $154 billion in 2025 sales across food, agriculture, financial and industrial divisions.", "The Cargill-MacMillan family collects an estimated 18% of net profits as dividends every year.", "He's one of nine billionaire siblings who inherited stakes in the company from their father John H.  MacMillan III, who died in 2008."], "forbes_facts": []}
